ts"],"id":"oewn-pioneer__2.36.00..","pos":"verb","src":"wn","sym":"47:1","syn":["open up"]},{"def":"take the lead or initiative in; participate in the development of","dna16":"8800105129000420","ex":["This South African surgeon pioneered heart transplants"],"id":"oewn-pioneer__2.36.01..","pos":"verb","src":"wn","sym":"","syn":["initiate"]},{"def":"open up and explore a new area","dna16":"8800105129000529","ex":["pioneer space"],"id":"oewn-pioneer__2.31.00..","pos":"verb","src":"wn","sym":"47:1","syn":[]},{"def":"One who goes before, as into the wilderness, preparing the way for others to follow.","dna16":"8800105129000628","ex":[],"id":"wikt:pioneer:noun:6","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"0:1,4:1","syn":[]},{"def":"A person or other entity who is first or among the earliest in any field of inquiry, enterprise, or progress.","dna16":"8800105129000727","ex":["Some people will consider their national heroes to be pioneers of civilization.","Certain politicians can be considered as pioneers of reform."],"id":"wikt:pioneer:noun:7","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"0:1,2:1,4:1,6:1,56:1","syn":[]},{"def":"A soldier detailed or employed to form roads, dig trenches, and make bridges, as an army advances; a sapper.","dna16":"8800105129000826","ex":[],"id":"wikt:pioneer:noun:8","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"A member of any of several European organizations advocating abstinence from alcohol.","dna16":"8800105129000925","ex":[],"id":"wikt:pioneer:noun:9","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"A member of a children’s organization operated by the Communist Party, typically in the second of three stages toward becoming a member of the Party itself.","dna16":"8800105129001022","ex":[],"id":"wikt:pioneer:noun:10","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"50:1,56:1","syn":[]},{"def":"To be the first to do or achieve (something), preparing the way for others to follow.","dna16":"8800105129001121","ex":["The young doctor pioneered a new life-saving surgical